      "text": "We need to convert the base 5 numbers \\(3124_5\\), \\(3122_5\\), and \\(124_5\\) to base 10 and then sum the results.\nTo convert the number \\(3124_5\\) to base 10, we use the formula for converting from base \\(b\\) to base \\(10\\):\n\\[ 3124_5 = 3 \\cdot 5^3 + 1 \\cdot 5^2 + 2 \\cdot 5^1 + 4 \\cdot 5^0 \\]\nCalculating each term separately, we get:\n\\[ 3 \\cdot 5^3 = 3 \\cdot 125 = 375 \\]\n\\[ 1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25 \\]\n\\[ 2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10 \\]\n\\[ 4 \\cdot 5^0 = 4 \\cdot 1 = 4 \\]\nAdding these values together, we get:\n\\[ 375 + 25 + 10 + 4 = 414 \\]\nSo, \\(3124_5 = 414_{10}\\).\n\nNext, we convert \\(3122_5\\) to base 10:\n\\[ 3122_5 = 3 \\cdot 5^3 + 1 \\cdot 5^2 + 2 \\cdot 5^1 + 2 \\cdot 5^0 \\]\nCalculating each term separately, we get:\n\\[ 3 \\cdot 5^3 = 3 \\cdot 125 = 375 \\]\n\\[ 1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25 \\]\n\\[ 2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10 \\]\n\\[ 2 \\cdot 5^0 = 2 \\cdot 1 = 2 \\]\nAdding these values together, we get:\n\\[ 375 + 25 + 10 + 2 = 412 \\]\nSo, \\(3122_5 = 412_{10}\\).\n\nFinally, we convert \\(124_5\\) to base 10:\n\\[ 124_5 = 1 \\cdot 5^2 + 2 \\cdot 5^1 + 4 \\cdot 5^0 \\]\nCalculating each term separately, we get:\n\\[ 1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25 \\]\n\\[ 2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10 \\]\n\\[ 4 \\cdot 5^0 = 4 \\cdot 1 = 4 \\]\nAdding these values together, we get:\n\\[ 25 + 10 + 4 = 39 \\]\nSo, \\(124_5 = 39_{10}\\).\n\nNow, we sum the base 10 equivalents of the base 5 numbers:\n\\[ 414_{10} + 412_{10} + 39_{10} = 865_{10} \\]\n\nThus, the total dollar amount that the pirate has accumulated is \\(\\boxed{865}\\).",
